From: Droidloom <droidloom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] power: no boot brightness override in Droidloom cells

Baseline: frameworks/base 94b4c163b7dfe5ce3607f7bb8456f9573f7de57d.

Until boot completes, PowerManagerService overrides the screen brightness
with the default one, to keep the bootloader's brightness steady. Display
brightness reports every override as a window's, and Droidloom's SystemUI
gives a window's level to the host's backlight: the host's screen flashed
to Android's default level for the last 100 ms of each start. A cell has
no bootloader picture, so its display takes the user's setting from the
start. The read-only Droidloom product marker confines this to Droidloom
cells.
diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/PowerManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/PowerManagerService.java
index 505530cc2..9da9bd64c 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/PowerManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/power/PowerManagerService.java
@@ -643,6 +643,13 @@ public final class PowerManagerService extends SystemService
     public final float mScreenBrightnessDefault;
     public final float mScreenBrightnessDim;
 
+    // The read-only product marker of Droidloom cells. A cell has no
+    // bootloader picture to keep steady during boot: its display takes the
+    // user's setting from the start, so only a window overrides it, and
+    // Droidloom's SystemUI gives a window's level to the host's backlight.
+    private static final boolean DROIDLOOM = SystemProperties.getBoolean(
+            "ro.vendor.droidloom.surfaceflinger_tasks", false);
+
     // Value we store for tracking face down behavior.
     @VisibleForTesting
     boolean mIsFaceDown = false;
@@ -4037,7 +4044,7 @@ public final class PowerManagerService extends SystemService
                 // Determine appropriate screen brightness.
                 final float screenBrightnessOverride;
                 CharSequence overrideTag = null;
-                if (!mBootCompleted) {
+                if (!mBootCompleted && !DROIDLOOM) {
                     // Keep the brightness steady during boot. This requires the
                     // bootloader brightness and the default brightness to be identical.
                     screenBrightnessOverride = mScreenBrightnessDefault;
